        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Red Queen's Race; Through the Looking-Glass; Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\n- People: Isaac Asimov; Lewis Carroll; Charles Lutwidge Dodgson\n- Concepts: Red Queen's race; science fiction; sequel\n\nFacts:\n- In 1865, Lewis Carroll published \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.\"\n- In 1871, Lewis Carroll, the pen name of Charles Lutwidge Dodgson, published \"Through the Looking-Glass, and What Alice Found There\" as the sequel to \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.\"\n- \"The Red Queen's Race\" is a science fiction short story by American writer Isaac Asimov.\n- Isaac Asimov's \"The Red Queen's Race\" uses the Red Queen's race from Lewis Carroll's \"Through the Looking-Glass\" as a metaphor for its final plot twist.",
